course: dictionary
lesson: 12777
title: Effectively
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Effectively» is an adverb. It tells you how something is done, or how true something really is. It has two main meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use.
explain: First meaning: in a way that works well and gets the result you want. «She used her time effectively and finished all her maths.» She got the result she wanted because she used her time well.
explain: Second meaning: in fact or really, even if not officially. «The game was effectively over when the rain started.» Nobody had blown the final whistle, but the game could not go on, so it was really over.
explain: A good check is to swap in «well» or «really». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Effectively means in a way that works well and gets the result you want.
fact: Effectively also means in fact or really, even if not officially.
fact: «Effectively» is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens or how true it is.
fact: Common phrases: work effectively, communicate effectively, and «effectively over».
fact: Context clues help: if the word praises good work, use the first meaning; if the word describes a real situation, use the second.
exercise: «The team worked effectively and won the match.» What does effectively mean here? | Very slowly and sadly | *In a way that works well and gets the result you want | In secret, without anyone knowing | In a rude and noisy way
exercise: «The rain had effectively ended the game.» What does effectively mean here? | *In fact, the game was really over | Happy and cheerful | Late, after the usual time | Officially, with a referee's signature
exercise: «Ella communicates effectively with her friends.» Which word tells us how Ella communicates? | *effectively | Ella | with | friends
test: «Mia planned her day effectively, so she had time to play.» What does effectively mean? | Sadly and slowly | Without any plan at all | *In a way that works well | Badly and in a rush
test: «The old tent was effectively a pile of rags after the storm.» What does effectively mean? | Officially, on paper | Happily and proudly | *In fact, it was really a pile of rags | Very brightly
exam: Jayden says effectively just means officially. Is he right? | Yes, it only means officially | Yes, it means happily | *No, it can mean working well, or really and in fact, even if not official | No, it means very loudly
